    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4476712": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics. Calumet College of St. Joseph. Description Position Summary Calumet College of St. Joseph (CCSJ) invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Mathematics beginning Spring 2026. Candidates must hold a master’s degree in mathematics or a closely related field and demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching within a liberal arts context. Preference will be given to applicants with experience teaching diverse undergraduate populations. The instructor may teach up to three courses per semester, including developmental, general education, and advanced mathematics, based on departmental needs. Most courses are scheduled Monday through Thursday between 8:30 a.m. and 2:15 p.m. The position is scheduled to begin in January 2027 for the Spring 2027 semester. Department of Biomedical and Health Sciences The Department of Biomedical and Health Sciences encompasses science and mathematics programs. The mathematics program offers a minor and supports general education and major-specific requirements. Faculty are expected to support student success through meaningful assessment, early intervention for at-risk students, and adherence to departmental policies. College Information CCSJ is a Catholic institution offering associate, bachelor’s, and master’s degrees. We foster a family-oriented environment and are committed to academic excellence and service. Faculty are expected to support the college’s mission: (https://www.ccsj.edu/about-ccsj/mission/) Requirements Application Requirements: Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three references. Final candidates will be asked to provide official transcripts. For more information contact, Dr. Carrie Hutton ( chutton@ccsj.edu ) or call 219-473-4284."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4636950": {
      "title": "Instructor of English",
      "description": "Instructor of English. Calumet College of St. Joseph. Description About Calumet College of St. Joseph: Calumet College of St. Joseph is a Catholic institution of higher learning dedicated to the academic, spiritual and ethical development of undergraduate and graduate students. Informed by the values of its founding religious community, the Missionaries of the Precious Blood (C.PP.S.), the College promotes the inherent dignity of all people, social justice, an ethic of service, student empowerment, opportunity, and lifelong learning. Located minutes from downtown Chicago and blocks from Lake Michigan, we offer a vibrant, affordable education in a stimulating learning environment. As the first recognized Hispanic-Serving college in Indiana, CCSJ has a tradition of embracing and celebrating diversity. For more information about the university and the department, visit us at https://www.ccsj.edu. Position Summary: English & Media Communications invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track position at the rank Instructor. We are seeking a generalist dedicated to excellence in undergraduate education, with primary responsibilities entailing teaching foundational and possibly advanced-level courses in literature and composition. Our ideal candidate will possess a multidisciplinary background that aligns with our department mission, which is centered around the concept of “story.” Specialization and/or prior experience instructing communications, theater, journalism, or broadcasting is highly desirable and will allow the successful candidate to contribute broadly to our diverse curriculum. Position Type: Full-Time, Non-Tenure Track (Renewable) Primary Responsibilities Teach a standard full-time (4/4) course load per semester, focusing primarily on first-year composition, introductory literature, and 200-level core story classes. Develop engaging, inclusive syllabi and course materials that support student success and retention. Provide regular, constructive feedback and mentorship to a diverse student population. Maintain regular office hours to support student learning outside the classroom. Participate in monthly EMCO program and Humanities department meetings. Participate in monthly Academic Senate meetings. Complete program service, which may include committee work, curriculum development, assessment initiatives, club advising, or student recruitment events. Perform other duties as assigned to advance program objectives, strengthen program visibility and reputation, and support enrollment, retention, and growth initiatives. Requirements Required Qualifications Master’s degree (M.A.) in English, Rhetoric and Composition, Literature, or a closely related field at the time of appointment (terminal degree, Ph.D. or M.F.A., preferred). Demonstrated experience and a record of excellence in teaching first-year composition and undergraduate literature courses. Commitment to working with diverse student populations and fostering an inclusive classroom environment. Desired Qualifications Academic specialization, professional experience, or prior university teaching experience in one or more of the following areas: Composition (e.g. two-semester, first-year sequence; advanced research composition) Literature (e.g. introductory, American/African American, Latin American, international, women’s, genre) Communications (e.g., media studies, public speaking, digital media, advertising) Theater (e.g., dramatic literature, performance, scriptwriting) Journalism (e.g., news writing, digital reporting, photojournalism) Broadcasting (e.g., audio/video production, podcasting, media writing) Experience with online or hybrid instructional delivery methods. Familiarity with writing program assessment or curriculum design. CCSJ is an equal opportunity employer and encourages candidates from traditionally underrepresented groups to apply. Successful applicants will demonstrate a commitment to the mission of CCSJ and the ability to work effectively with individuals and groups from diverse backgrounds. Please note that CCSJ is not able to sponsor or transfer employment visas now or in the future. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout their employment. Employment at Calumet College of St. Joseph is contingent upon proof of eligibility to work in the United States, verification of education/credentials, and a background check."
    }
